        "prompt": "State the domain of $f$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$D_f=(-\\infty,-1)\\cup(-1,2)\\cup(2,\\infty)$.",
          "worked": "$$x^2-x-2=(x-2)(x+1).$$\nThe original denominator is zero at $x=-1$ and $x=2$, so both values are excluded.\n$$D_f=(-\\infty,-1)\\cup(-1,2)\\cup(2,\\infty).$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p90-q49-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Graph $y=f(x)$, showing all important features.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p90-q49-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "y=\\frac{x+2}{x-2}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", with ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x\\ne-1,\\ x\\ne2",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ". Asymptotes: ",
